  "contract": "For actuated histories, unavailable or unusable screened/before-world references produce a semantic finding. Present nonblank strings are compared exactly without normalization or a new SHA-format grammar. Unfinished nonactuated, empty, reject-only and unknown-kind histories keep existing behavior. This is an explicit completeness tightening of historical available-link checking, not a claim that all legacy omissions were previously forbidden.",
  "chain_construction": "For each row event i: set seq=i, prev_hash=previous event_hash or64zeroes; hash SHA256(prev ASCII + LF + json.dumps(event,sort_keys=True,separators=(',',':'),ensure_ascii=False).encode('utf-8')); append event_hash. All listed fixture events are therefore validly rehashed before product receiving. No fixture comes from live actuation.",
  "receiving": "Run exact baseline/candidate replay_audit and unchanged decision_trace.review_trace plus actual main(argv) with captured stdin/stdout/stderr; this is in-process CLI-entry receiving, not independent OS-child/native/UI receiving. Report counters, complete JSON, findings, source/input immutability and original mismatched-link diagnostic preservation. Bound local execution to fixed case set; no filesystem or actuation calls.",
